// GRH as the manuscript deduces it — the dependency structure, machine-checked.
//
// WHAT THIS IS. "The Music of the Primes" (Masullo, draft released 2026-11-20) proves a
// Trace Formula and asserts GRH as its consequence. The chapter that would carry out that
// deduction, Chapter 13, is a two-page stub: Theorem 13.3.1.2's statement is the author's
// footnote "Insert statement". The deduction exists only as a prose OUTLINE in §1.4.
//
// So this file formalizes §1.4's chain. Every step is a `hole`, and the two KINDS of hole
// encode OUR WORKLIST, not the manuscript's:
//
//   hole X                        (bare) the manuscript PROVES this. It is ours to
//                                 transcribe, so strict check must REJECT it — that keeps
//                                 it on the worklist until the proof is actually written in
//                                 2b4m. Walk these backwards into the manuscript and fill
//                                 them in.
//
//   hole X cites "manuscript …"   a TRUE GAP in the released text: nothing there
//                                 establishes it. We assume it pending work by the author,
//                                 and the citation records exactly what we are assuming and
//                                 why. Strict check PASSES these, disclosed.
//
// So `2b4m check` failing is the NORMAL state here, and its output is the transcription
// backlog. `--axioms` separates the two kinds: bare holes are ours, cited holes are the
// author's. When every bare hole is discharged, what remains is precisely the list to send
// him.
//
// The encoding is deliberately COARSE. Zeros, test functions and L-functions are opaque
// sorts and predicates; no analysis is modelled. That is the right altitude for the
// question being asked — "does the cited chain reach GRH, and what is missing?" — and it
// keeps every hole's statement readable against the manuscript. A real formalization of
// the ANALYSIS would be a different (vastly larger) undertaking.

theory vocab <<< "shared/vocabulary.b4m"
theory trace <<< "trace-formula/trace-formula.b4m"

// The shared vocabulary, declared ONCE in shared/vocabulary.b4m and aliased here. Identity
// in 2b4m is by ORIGIN, not spelling: redeclaring `TestFunction` locally would make it a
// DIFFERENT sort from the trace-formula layer's, and the citation below could not typecheck.
sort Zero = vocab.Zero
sort TestFunction = vocab.TestFunction
pred onTheCriticalLine = vocab.onTheCriticalLine
pred isNonTrivialZero = vocab.isNonTrivialZero
pred vanishesOnTheNormOneIdeles = vocab.vanishesOnTheNormOneIdeles
pred isTestFunction = vocab.isTestFunction
pred isAMollifiedPowerApproximant = vocab.isAMollifiedPowerApproximant
pred theTraceFormulaHoldsAt = vocab.theTraceFormulaHoldsAt
pred theNonArchimedeanSumComputesTheLogDerivative = vocab.theNonArchimedeanSumComputesTheLogDerivative
pred theLogDerivativeIsHolomorphicOffTheCentralPoint = vocab.theLogDerivativeIsHolomorphicOffTheCentralPoint
pred noZerosRightOfTheCriticalLine = vocab.noZerosRightOfTheCriticalLine
pred noZerosLeftOfTheCriticalLine = vocab.noZerosLeftOfTheCriticalLine

intheory generalizedRiemannHypothesis

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// OURS TO TRANSCRIBE — each is stated AND proved in the released manuscript, so each is a
// BARE hole: strict check rejects it, and it stays on the worklist until transcribed.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

// CLOSED. Theorem 12.5.1.1, p. 519 — the declared main theorem. This was a bare hole; it is
// now PROVED one layer down in trace-formula/, from the manuscript's own proof skeleton, so
// here it is a citation. Its own six dependencies are the new frontier.
fact theTraceFormula = trace.theTraceFormula

// §1.4.2 constructs the approximants explicitly (mollifier ρ_ε, bump h) and §1.4.3 bounds
// the Archimedean integrals uniformly, so Montel applies. The CONSTRUCTION is written out;
// what is NOT written out is that the limit interchange is valid (see the bare holes).
hole theMollifiedApproximantsExist:
  exists f: TestFunction;
  isTestFunction(f) and vanishesOnTheNormOneIdeles(f) and isAMollifiedPowerApproximant(f)

// Theorem B.7.2.1 / B.7.2.4, Euler products on the 1-line. §1.7.2 lists non-vanishing on
// the 1-line as "used as an input throughout".
hole theEulerProductsOnTheOneLine:
  theLogDerivativeIsHolomorphicOffTheCentralPoint() ->
  noZerosRightOfTheCriticalLine()

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// TRUE GAPS IN THE MANUSCRIPT — assumed pending work by the author. Each carries a `cites`
// recording what is being assumed and why nothing in the released text supplies it, so
// strict check passes them while disclosing them. These are the list to send the author.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

// §1.4.3-1.4.4. The author identifies this as the hard part in his own words: the
// non-Archimedean integrals "are infinitely many, and they are the source of all the
// difficulties: their sum approximates L'_f(s+1/2, χ)/L_f(s+1/2, χ)". Montel gives a
// subsequence along which the ARCHIMEDEAN integrals converge uniformly; that the
// infinite non-Archimedean sum also passes to the limit is asserted, not proved.
hole theLimitInterchangeIsValid
  cites "NOT IN THE RELEASED TEXT — assumed pending the author. Ch. 13 (which would prove it) is a 2-page stub; the author himself calls the infinite non-Archimedean sum 'the source of all the difficulties' (§1.4.3). Montel gives uniform convergence of the finitely many ARCHIMEDEAN integrals only":
  forall f: TestFunction;
  isAMollifiedPowerApproximant(f) -> theTraceFormulaHoldsAt(f) ->
  theNonArchimedeanSumComputesTheLogDerivative(f)

// §1.4.5, "Putting everything together". Cites "§5.1" for the assembly, but §5.1 is "The
// topological vector spaces of adelic theta-functions and Idelic Z-functions" — a stale
// reference, so the justification is not located in the released text. Two `Finish!`
// footnotes (the author's own) also attach to §1.4's Trace Formula statement.
hole theLogDerivativeHasOnlyTheCentralPole
  cites "NOT IN THE RELEASED TEXT — assumed pending the author. §1.4.5 asserts it and cites '§5.1', but §5.1 is about topological vector spaces (a stale reference); two of the author's own 'Finish!' footnotes attach here":
  forall f: TestFunction;
  theNonArchimedeanSumComputesTheLogDerivative(f) ->
  theLogDerivativeIsHolomorphicOffTheCentralPoint()

// The functional-equation reflection. Stated in one line in §1.4.5 ("so by the functional
// equation the same holds for L(s, χ) over C_{<1/2}"); the manuscript has the functional
// equation, but this deduction is not written out.
hole theFunctionalEquationReflectsTheZeroFreeRegion
  cites "NOT IN THE RELEASED TEXT — assumed pending the author. One line in §1.4.5 ('so by the functional equation the same holds over C_{<1/2}'); the functional equation IS in the manuscript, this deduction from it is not written out":
  noZerosRightOfTheCriticalLine() -> noZerosLeftOfTheCriticalLine()

// The final step. No zeros strictly either side of the critical line leaves every
// non-trivial zero ON it. Trivial as real analysis, but it is the content of Theorem
// 13.3.1.2, whose statement in the released text is the footnote "Insert statement".
hole everyZeroOffTheLineIsExcluded
  cites "NOT IN THE RELEASED TEXT — assumed pending the author. This IS Theorem 13.3.1.2, whose statement in the released draft is the author's footnote 'Insert statement'":
  noZerosRightOfTheCriticalLine() -> noZerosLeftOfTheCriticalLine() ->
  forall r: Zero; isNonTrivialZero(r) -> onTheCriticalLine(r)

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// THE DEDUCTION. Every step is kernel-checked; the holes above are its only assumptions.
// `--axioms` on this theorem prints the exact dependency list.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

theorem generalizedRiemannHypothesis: forall r: Zero;
  isNonTrivialZero(r) -> onTheCriticalLine(r)
proof
  @an-approximant-exists |
    exists f: TestFunction;
      isTestFunction(f) and vanishesOnTheNormOneIdeles(f) and isAMollifiedPowerApproximant(f)
    [by cite theMollifiedApproximantsExist]
  @from-the-approximant |
    unpack phi: TestFunction from an-approximant-exists {
      @phi-properties |
        isTestFunction(phi) and vanishesOnTheNormOneIdeles(phi) and isAMollifiedPowerApproximant(phi)
        [by hypothesis from-the-approximant]
      // `and` is LEFT-associative, so the conjunction is (A and B) and C.
      @phi-head |
        isTestFunction(phi) and vanishesOnTheNormOneIdeles(phi)
        [by and_lhs phi-properties]
      @phi-is-a-test-function |
        isTestFunction(phi)
        [by and_lhs phi-head]
      @phi-vanishes |
        vanishesOnTheNormOneIdeles(phi)
        [by and_rhs phi-head]
      @phi-is-an-approximant |
        isAMollifiedPowerApproximant(phi)
        [by and_rhs phi-properties]

      // Trace Formula at phi (Thm 12.5.1.1), using its standing hypothesis
      @trace-all |
        forall f: TestFunction;
          isTestFunction(f) -> vanishesOnTheNormOneIdeles(f) -> theTraceFormulaHoldsAt(f)
        [by cite theTraceFormula]
      @trace-at-phi-needs-vanishing |
        isTestFunction(phi) -> vanishesOnTheNormOneIdeles(phi) -> theTraceFormulaHoldsAt(phi)
        [by apply_at(phi) trace-all]
      @trace-at-phi-needs-only-vanishing |
        vanishesOnTheNormOneIdeles(phi) -> theTraceFormulaHoldsAt(phi)
        [by modus_ponens trace-at-phi-needs-vanishing phi-is-a-test-function]
      @trace-holds |
        theTraceFormulaHoldsAt(phi)
        [by modus_ponens trace-at-phi-needs-only-vanishing phi-vanishes]

      // the limit interchange (TRUE GAP) extracts L'/L
      @interchange-all |
        forall f: TestFunction;
          isAMollifiedPowerApproximant(f) -> theTraceFormulaHoldsAt(f) ->
          theNonArchimedeanSumComputesTheLogDerivative(f)
        [by cite theLimitInterchangeIsValid]
      @interchange-at-phi |
        isAMollifiedPowerApproximant(phi) -> theTraceFormulaHoldsAt(phi) ->
          theNonArchimedeanSumComputesTheLogDerivative(phi)
        [by apply_at(phi) interchange-all]
      @interchange-needs-trace |
        theTraceFormulaHoldsAt(phi) -> theNonArchimedeanSumComputesTheLogDerivative(phi)
        [by modus_ponens interchange-at-phi phi-is-an-approximant]
      @log-derivative-computed |
        theNonArchimedeanSumComputesTheLogDerivative(phi)
        [by modus_ponens interchange-needs-trace trace-holds]

      // holomorphy off the central point (TRUE GAP)
      @holomorphy-all |
        forall f: TestFunction;
          theNonArchimedeanSumComputesTheLogDerivative(f) ->
          theLogDerivativeIsHolomorphicOffTheCentralPoint()
        [by cite theLogDerivativeHasOnlyTheCentralPole]
      @holomorphy-at-phi |
        theNonArchimedeanSumComputesTheLogDerivative(phi) ->
          theLogDerivativeIsHolomorphicOffTheCentralPoint()
        [by apply_at(phi) holomorphy-all]
      @holomorphic |
        theLogDerivativeIsHolomorphicOffTheCentralPoint()
        [by modus_ponens holomorphy-at-phi log-derivative-computed]

      // no zeros to the right (grounded: Euler products on the 1-line)
      @right-implication |
        theLogDerivativeIsHolomorphicOffTheCentralPoint() -> noZerosRightOfTheCriticalLine()
        [by cite theEulerProductsOnTheOneLine]
      @no-zeros-right |
        noZerosRightOfTheCriticalLine()
        [by modus_ponens right-implication holomorphic]

      // reflect across the line (TRUE GAP)
      @reflection |
        noZerosRightOfTheCriticalLine() -> noZerosLeftOfTheCriticalLine()
        [by cite theFunctionalEquationReflectsTheZeroFreeRegion]
      @no-zeros-left |
        noZerosLeftOfTheCriticalLine()
        [by modus_ponens reflection no-zeros-right]

      // conclude (TRUE GAP: this IS Theorem 13.3.1.2)
      @exclusion |
        noZerosRightOfTheCriticalLine() -> noZerosLeftOfTheCriticalLine() ->
          forall r: Zero; isNonTrivialZero(r) -> onTheCriticalLine(r)
        [by cite everyZeroOffTheLineIsExcluded]
      @exclusion-needs-left |
        noZerosLeftOfTheCriticalLine() ->
          forall r: Zero; isNonTrivialZero(r) -> onTheCriticalLine(r)
        [by modus_ponens exclusion no-zeros-right]
      @grh-inner |
        forall r: Zero; isNonTrivialZero(r) -> onTheCriticalLine(r)
        [by modus_ponens exclusion-needs-left no-zeros-left]
    }
  @conclusion |
    forall r: Zero; isNonTrivialZero(r) -> onTheCriticalLine(r)
    [by unpacked from-the-approximant]
qed
